    "title": "Raptors set Toronto franchise record with massive season-opening win - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Billy Heyen ,\n1 hours ago\nThe Toronto Raptors didn't waste much time getting their season rolling.\nThey took a lead after a quarter on the Atlanta Hawks , pulled away in the third and won the game, 138-118, to open the campaign with a win on Wednesday night in Atlanta.\nIn the process, the Raptors set a franchise record. This was the largest margin of victory in a season opener in franchise history, according to Sportsnet .\nThe Raptors had seven players score in double figures in the process.\nMORE: VJ Edgecombe scored most points in NBA debut since Wilt Chamberlain in 1959\nRJ Barrett led the way with 25 points to go with eight rebounds and five assists while shooting 9-for-12 from the floor.\nScottie Barnes scored 22 on 9-for-14 shooting with six rebounds and nine assists.\nOff the bench, Gradey Dick contributed a rapid-fire 21 points.\nMORE: Giannis in 3rd place in NBA history on impressive list behind Kareem, Oscar\nBrandon Ingram dropped 16 points in his Raptors debut, also grabbing nine rebounds.\nJakob Poeltl was an uber-efficient 7-of-8 for a total of 14 points\nImmanuel Quickly rounded out the double-figure scorers in the starting lineup with 13 points, to go with 8 assists.\nAnd off the bench, Jamal Shead worked his way to 10 points.\nIt's quite the group, and quite the result. The Raptors will be hoping they're not a one-tricky pony and can run this back.\nMore NBA News: Zion Williamson makes 2 pieces of NBA history to open season Steph Curry and Jimmy Butler have a season-long bet Davion Mitchell played a season opener unlike any in Miami Heat history It didn't take Draymond Green long to get his first technical foul of the season Alperen Sengun puts up eye-popping career high in season opener for Rockets Hornets set an incredible 9-player NBA record to open the season",
